From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kk: reject render pipelines whose vertex function does not resolve

STEAMAC-BN/BP (1.9.14, Apple M2, macOS 27.2.0, CS2): the VM process
aborted in Metal's render pipeline descriptor validation, "vertexFunction
must not be nil", under mtl_new_render_pipeline (kk_draw <-
kk_CmdDrawIndexedIndirect2KHR). A library function descriptor carries
only a name: when the library has no vertex function of that name,
Metal resolves it to nil and aborts the process even though an NSError
pointer is passed. The reports carry no MSL, so the program that named a
missing function is not known yet.

Resolve the vertex function before creating the pipeline. A missing,
non-vertex or absent function fails the pipeline like any other compile
failure (the cache drops the reservation; the draw path already handles
a NULL pipeline) and logs the name, the library's functions and, from
kk_compile_graphics_pipeline, the stage, entry points and MSL hashes of
the program, so the next report names it.

Regression: REPRO_CASE=sentry-bn REPRO_DRIVER=kosmickrisp
host/moltenvk/repro/run.sh <dylib> calls the driver's
mtl_new_render_pipeline with a missing, fragment-stage and absent vertex
function: the 1.9.14 driver aborts on the first; with this patch all
three return NULL and a valid pair draws 16 green pixels.

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_compiler.m b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_compiler.m
index 9aab72f..0f73b35 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_compiler.m
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_compiler.m
@@ -366,6 +366,30 @@
       id<MTL4Compiler> comp = (id<MTL4Compiler>)compiler;
       MTL4RenderPipelineDescriptor *desc = (MTL4RenderPipelineDescriptor *)descriptor;
 
+      /* A library function descriptor is only a name. When it names no vertex
+       * function of its library, Metal resolves it to a nil vertexFunction
+       * and aborts the process in render pipeline descriptor validation even
+       * though an error pointer is passed (STEAMAC-BN/BP). Resolve it first
+       * and fail the pipeline like any other compile failure. */
+      MTL4LibraryFunctionDescriptor *vertex =
+         (MTL4LibraryFunctionDescriptor *)desc.vertexFunctionDescriptor;
+      id<MTLFunction> function = vertex != nil && vertex.library != nil && vertex.name != nil
+                                    ? [vertex.library newFunctionWithName:vertex.name]
+                                    : nil;
+      const MTLFunctionType type = function != nil ? function.functionType : (MTLFunctionType)0;
+      [function release];
+      if (type != MTLFunctionTypeVertex) {
+         NSArray<NSString *> *names = vertex.library.functionNames;
+         fprintf(stderr,
+                 "kk: render pipeline rejected: vertex function \"%s\" %s in its library "
+                 "(%lu function(s), first \"%s\")\n",
+                 vertex.name != nil ? vertex.name.UTF8String : "(none)",
+                 function != nil ? "is not a vertex function" : "not found",
+                 (unsigned long)names.count,
+                 names.count != 0 ? names.firstObject.UTF8String : "");
+         return NULL;
+      }
+
       struct mtl_compile c;
       mtl_compile_begin(&c, compiler, "render", 2u);
       NSError *error = nil;
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index af97042..acf465a 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -2194,6 +2194,13 @@ kk_compile_graphics_pipeline(struct kk_device *device, mtl_compiler *compiler,
       /* Takes the key, which this caller no longer owns */
       kk_metal_cache_publish(&device->metal_render_pipelines, key, render);
       if (render == NULL) {
+         /* Names the program for the bridge's failure line (STEAMAC-BN/BP) */
+         mesa_loge("kk: render pipeline failed: %s entry %s MSL %08x, fragment "
+                   "entry %s MSL %08x, stages 0x%x",
+                   _mesa_shader_stage_to_abbrev(vs_stage),
+                   vs_data->entrypoint_name, _mesa_hash_string(vs_data->code),
+                   fs_data->entrypoint_name, _mesa_hash_string(fs_data->code),
+                   vs->info.vs.additional_stages_bits);
          mtl_release(fragment_library);
          mtl_release(vertex_library);
          return VK_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER_NV;
